/E (Question. How did published polling averages and Polymarket prices follow the 2026 US Senate races, how closely did they move together, and how well did each call the results? The study began as a ranking of pollster accuracy. Polling data proved too fragmented for that, so it was reframed as a comparison of two public information sources about the same races.)
