/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 442 0 R
/T (Interpretation. Polls and markets carry much of the same information about which races favour which party, and they differ most in close races and in how they price uncertainty. The main fact about accuracy in this cycle is a common error of about 4.5 points toward the Democrats, which the market shared. Neither source can be called the better forecaster from this evidence.)
/E (Interpretation. Polls and markets carry much of the same information about which races favour which party, and they differ most in close races and in how they price uncertainty. The main fact about accuracy in this cycle is a common error of about 4.5 points toward the Democrats, which the market shared. Neither source can be called the better forecaster from this evidence.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
567 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 442 0 R
/T (Limitations. The study covers one election and 12 to 16 states whose errors move together. Results are unofficial until certified. Poll-to-probability conversions rely on assumed forecast errors. Polls are equal-weighted with no house-effect adjustment. Several tests were added after earlier results were seen and are labelled exploratory. All findings are descriptive and none shows causation.)
/E (Limitations. The study covers one election and 12 to 16 states whose errors move together. Results are unofficial until certified. Poll-to-probability conversions rely on assumed forecast errors. Polls are equal-weighted with no house-effect adjustment. Several tests were added after earlier results were seen and are labelled exploratory. All findings are descriptive and none shows causation.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
