696 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 448 0 R
/E (This makes them particularly useful for examining how expectations about an election result evolve over time. Nevertheless, the price should be understood as an implied market probability rather than a direct measurement of the objective probability of an event occurring.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
697 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 448 0 R
/T (1.3 Polymarket and Political Elections)
/E (1.3 Polymarket and Political Elections)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
698 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 448 0 R
/E (Political elections provide a particularly relevant application of prediction markets because election outcomes are uncertain events that attract substantial public attention and generate a continuous flow of information. During an election cycle, participants may revise their expectations in response to opinion polls, candidate announcements, campaign developments, debates, endorsements, fundraising information, economic conditions, and other political or social events. These developments can influence the willingness of participants to buy or sell contracts, leading to changes in market prices.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
699 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 448 0 R
/E (In an electoral market, a contract may ask whether a particular candidate or political party will win an election or a specific legislative seat. A YES share therefore represents a position tied to the occurrence of that defined outcome. If the contract concerns whether the Democratic Party will win a particular Senate seat, its price provides an indication of the market's assessment of the likelihood of that party winning the seat. This is distinct from a market asking which individual candidate will win, since the precise contract wording determines the event being measured.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
700 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 448 0 R
/E (The value of examining these markets over an election cycle lies not only in their final prices but also in how those prices change as new information becomes available. A movement in a Democratic Party YES contract, for example, may reflect a change in participants' expectations following a newly released poll or another political development. The market thus provides a continuously updated series of prices that can be examined alongside traditional polling data.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
701 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 448 0 R
/E (However, prediction-market prices are not produced through a representative sample of voters. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
