/E (Results come from the CivicAPI United States Senate file \(race 87528\), retrieved on November 11, 2026 \(09:03 UTC\) with 93.7% of votes reporting overall. Election results: civicAPI \(https://civicapi.org\), credited as its terms require. civicAPI describes its counts as unofficial until they are certified. 34 of 35 races carry a call. Alaska has none \(Peltola ahead by 1.75 points with 83.8% reporting\) and is not scored. Mississippi \(Colom ahead by 0.32 points with 98.5% reporting\) is the narrowest of the called races. The compiled DeepSyte file was also checked: it holds primaries, runoffs and special elections through September 15, 2026 but no general-election rows, so it is not used for results. CivicAPI marks calls but not who made them, and counts are provisional \(reporting ranges from about 75% to 99% by state\). We use civicAPI's call flags as given and rerun Analysis 4 when counts are final or certified.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
