/E (Reading the results. Polls and markets agree strongly on the ranking of races, but short-run changes in poll averages show no detectable relation to short-run price changes. The two-month result suggests the weak short-run signal is mostly noise in poll averages, not indifference by the market \(Section 5.1.9\). The analysis is observational and does not show causation.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
