871 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 461 0 R
/E (The weekly, four-week and lead-lag tests use a complete grid for each state: one date every 7 days \(every 28 days for the four-week test\), starting at the state's first poll-average date and running to Nov 2. Every weekly change therefore spans exactly seven days, and every four-week change exactly 28 days. A change in the market is the difference in log-odds between two grid dates. A change in the polls is the difference in the polling average between the same dates, and both endpoints must have at least k surveys in the window. The within-state levels tests also use weekly dates: Table 3 uses each state's own weekly grid, and Table 4 puts all states on one common weekly calendar \(every 7 days from Jan 2, 2026\).)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
