/E (A longer horizon should raise the signal relative to noise. We use a complete four-week grid \(21-day window, at least one survey at both endpoints; k = 3 leaves too few observations\) and relate the poll change to the market change over the same four weeks and over the following four weeks \(Table 2\). All four estimates are close to zero. They are also imprecise, because only 33 to 53 state-periods are available, so they neither confirm nor rule out a modest relationship.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [2]
>>
