1054 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 477 0 R
/E (Polls and prediction markets agree on the ranking of Senate races, with a stable relationship from October, and the agreement strengthens when polling is dense. They show no robust relationship in week-to-week or four-week changes, and the lead-lag pattern is too weak and too dependent on dating to be treated as evidence. Within-state levels are positively related but not robustly so. Over two months, cumulative changes do line up across states, which is consistent with noise rather than indifference explaining the short-run null. This baseline is the starting point for the disagreement \(Analysis 2\), poll-release \(Analysis 3\), forecast-accuracy \(Analysis 4\) and methodology \(Analysis 5\) analyses.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
