/E (Approach. Polls and prices are both estimates of who will win. Each week we fit, across the competitive states, the relationship between the market's log-odds and the poll margin. The fitted line is the probability that the polls alone imply for a given margin. A state's disagreement is how far its market price sits from that line.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [4]
>>
