/P 480 0 R
/E (A gap is substantial if it is at least 15 probability points or at least 3 margin points. The 15-point threshold was set before any output was examined. The 3-point threshold was set after seeing a first output, as roughly one survey's sampling error. A later calculation from the notebook puts the median standard error of a single survey margin in this sample at 3.3 points \(Section 5.1.9\), close to the cutoff. A state is a persistent disagreement if its margin gap reaches 3 points in at least 60% of the weeks in which it appears in a fit. The 60% share is also a judgment, so Table 8 reports how the result changes with both cutoffs. Weeks on opposite sides are counted separately.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [3]
