1100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 481 0 R
/E (A first version fitted every state with at least two surveys \(at least eight states per date\). Its gaps were strongly correlated with the poll margin among the competitive states \(r = 0.60, n = 107 state-weeks\), which means the pooled line was too flat. The saturated states \(Massachusetts, Rhode Island, Arkansas and Montana\), whose prices are pinned near 0% or 100%, pulled the common slope down to about 0.2 \(Table 1\) and made several competitive states appear to disagree when they did not. A correlation between gap and margin across all state-weeks cannot detect this, because it is zero by construction for a least-squares fit. The saturated states are excluded because the log-odds conversion is unstable near the boundaries.)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
