1102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 481 0 R
/E (Two rules picked states for closer study, applied after the output was seen but before any state was compared with its result: a gap of 15 or more probability points in at least half of a state's weeks, or the poll average and the market on opposite sides in at least half of its weeks. Kansas and Minnesota meet the first rule \(7 of 7 and 5 of 9 weeks\), Kansas also meets the second \(6 of 7 weeks\), and Iowa meets the second \(5 of 10 weeks\). All three are carried to Analysis 4 as focus cases, and all 12 competitive states are compared with their results regardless.)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1103 0 obj
<<
