/T (No state meets the persistent-disagreement rule as set \(a gap of 3 or more margin points in at least 60% of weeks\). The result depends on the two cutoffs \(Table 8\). Minnesota qualifies if the required share is relaxed to 50%, at either a 3-point or a 4-point threshold. At a 2-point threshold Kansas and Minnesota qualify at shares of 60% and 70%, and South Carolina joins them at 50%. Under the rule as set, Minnesota comes closest, with a gap of 3 or more margin points in 5 of 9 weeks \(56%\). Across all 107 state-weeks, 85% have a gap smaller than 3 margin points, and in 11 of the 12 states the mean gap is within 2.3 margin points.)
