<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3341 0 R
/E (The 3-point threshold was set after a first output was seen, so we use a threshold rule and not a significance test. The standard error of a survey margin is computed assuming simple random sampling, which ignores design effects, so polls look more precise than they are. Real poll error is larger than sampling error: Analysis 4 finds a shared miss of about 4.5 points.)
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [9]
>>
