1193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 489 0 R
/E (Polls and the market agree closely when the benchmark is fitted on competitive states, especially from mid-October. A tied poll average was priced at 41% to 44.5% for the Democrat from mid-September, a small and stable shading toward the Republican. No state shows persistent disagreement under the rule as set, though Minnesota qualifies if the required share is relaxed to 50%. Minnesota \(market more Democratic than the polls imply\) and Kansas \(market less Democratic\) stand out, and Iowa meets one selection rule through the 50% line. All three go to Analysis 4, where the results show whether the market or the polls were closer.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
