/E (The events are surveys in the 16 analysis states, one per survey \(452 in all; a survey listed under several poll IDs counts once\), using the nominee-pair margins from Section 4.2. An event is usable if it has a publication time, at least one earlier survey from the same state that ended in the previous 21 days \(to define a prior average\), and a price window that ends by Nov 2. That leaves 11 events with an exact time and 69 with a date only. The competitive subgroup holds 68 of the 69 date-only events, so it is nearly the same sample.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [4]
