<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 500 0 R
/E (Only 15 of 452 surveys have an exact publication time, so the planned hour-level windows cannot be run, and the analysis rests on 69 events with a release date. On those events, prices moved in the direction of a poll's surprise: about +0.016 log-odds per point. Prices were more active around releases than on other days, and the slope is near zero in windows before the release, so the pattern is not a pre-existing trend. The evidence is moderate and exploratory, and it is consistent in size with the weekly slopes in Analysis 1.)
/Pg 70 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
