1410 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 506 0 R
/E (A first pass \(Nov 7 to 9\) mixed races with a known winner only and races with vote shares in one table, so the printed sample size \(16\) overstated the races behind the error statistics \(9\). It also used figures from Wikipedia and news reports. Results were then taken from the single civicAPI source under the rules above. Four parts of the original protocol were not run: log loss, state-level bootstrap intervals, a version of the poll average that requires at least two surveys, and a comparison with and without races within 1.0 point of a tie. A later check found that Montana's Democratic-minus-Republican poll margin had entered the poll-based winner and Brier comparisons although its result is not head-to-head. Those comparisons were then restricted to the 15 head-to-head races.)
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
