1517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 516 0 R
/E (The main fact about accuracy in this cycle is the common miss of about 4.5 points toward the Democrats. The market shared it, and its lean toward the Republicans in close races put it further from the outcome than the polls. The roughly one-point shading toward the Republicans that Analysis 2 found therefore pointed the wrong way, and Kansas, where the market sat below the poll-implied probability, is a case in which the polls were closer to the result. This analysis describes accuracy. It does not test whether one source is better. This differs from Vaughan Williams and Reade \(2016\), who find markets more accurate over many US elections; our comparison covers one cycle and uses polls without bias correction.)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
