1537 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 517 0 R
/E (Polls and markets named the same number of winners on the final day \(13 of 15 head-to-head analysis states\), missed the same two near-ties, and the market also missed Kansas until the last day. Poll averages converted with an assumed forecast error scored better than market prices at every horizon, mainly because the market priced the close races well below 50% and the Democrats won them. The Democrats beat the final poll average in all 15 head-to-head races, by 4.52 points on average, and most of that miss was common to every state. These are provisional counts from one election, and the comparison is descriptive.)
/Pg 87 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
