1654 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 527 0 R
/E (Co-movement. Polls and markets agreed strongly on which states favoured which party. On November 1 their rankings across 15 states had a Spearman correlation of 0.96. Agreement over time within states was weaker. Week-to-week and four-week changes showed no reliable relationship. Within-state levels were positively related but not robustly so. Over the two months from September 1 to November 1, cumulative changes did line up across states \(slope +0.10, Spearman 0.82\), but this test was added after the weekly results were seen and weakened for shorter spans. We read the pattern as a clear agreement on levels and little detectable agreement on short-run changes, most plausibly because changes in thin poll averages are mostly noise. It is not evidence that markets ignore polls.)
/Pg 97 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
