/T (There was also a stable common offset: a tied poll average was priced at 40% to 45% for the Democrat, equivalent to shading the margin 0.6 to 1.1 points toward the Republican. This analysis cannot say whether that reflects state partisanship, a house effect in the polls, or a general Republican prior.)
/E (There was also a stable common offset: a tied poll average was priced at 40% to 45% for the Democrat, equivalent to shading the margin 0.6 to 1.1 points toward the Republican. This analysis cannot say whether that reflects state partisanship, a house effect in the polls, or a general Republican prior.)
/Pg 98 0 R
